## Why This Is Asked

Explores data residency, cross-tenant sharing, auditability, and lineage in OTCA-structured systems. Candidates must design a scalable data model, streaming topology, and testing plan that enforce per-tenant residency while enabling compliant cross-tenant workflows.

## Key Concepts

- OTCA residency and policy enforcement
- Data lineage modeling and immutable auditing
- Event streaming and regional data stores
- Token-based cross-tenant sharing with expiry

## Code Example

```javascript
// Policy evaluation stub for cross-tenant access
function evaluateToken(token, context) {
  if (!token || token.expiresAt < Date.now()) {
    return { allowed: false, reason: 'Token expired or invalid' };
  }
  if (token.tenantId !== context.targetTenantId) {
    return { allowed: false, reason: 'Cross-tenant violation' };
  }
  return { allowed: true, scope: token.scope };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of privacy-first telemetry with per-tenant policies, plus practical exposure to a lightweight streaming path and simple data governance.

## Key Concepts

- Ingestion-time redaction and policy evaluation
- Per-tenant governance and allow/drop decisions
- Region-based streaming topology and partitioned storage
- Dashboard freshness and SLAs

## Code Example

```javascript
function redactPayload(tenantId, payload, policyMap){
  const policy = policyMap[tenantId] || {};
  const redacted = {...payload};
  if(policy.redactPII){
    if('device_id' in redacted) redacted.device_id = 'REDACTED';
    if('location' in redacted) redacted.location = 'REDACTED';
  }
  if(policy.allowedEvents && !policy.allowedEvents.includes(payload.event_type)){
    return null; // drop
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

